          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Where an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of morphisms between any two objects, a
            = succeed "." do
              %em hom-space
          %p
            There are several ways to
            %em present
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            by an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with some extra structure: for instance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            may be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            or even a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}\mathbf{C}(X,Y)
            that presents the hom-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}(X,Y)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            – is called the
            %em derived hom space
            or
            %em homotopy function complex
            and denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom(X,Y)
            or similarly.
          %h2#presentations Presentations
          %p
            There are many ways to present an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic data
          %p
            The most basic data is that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ForACategoryWithWeakEquivalences"} For a category with weak equivalences
          %p
            Particularly useful extra structure on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            that helps with computing the derived hom spaces is the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %em framings
            – that generalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+objects"} cylinder objects
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+objects"} path objects
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Framings"} For a model category
          %p
            Still a bit more helpful structure on top of a bare model category is that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+objects"} hom objects
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#EnrichedHomsCofToFib"} For a simplicial model category
          %h3#ForACategoryWithWeakEquivalences For a category with weak equivalences
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W \subset Mor(C))
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
          #ZigZagCategories.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Fix
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Obj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Obj(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi wMor
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} wMor_C^n(X,Y)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  whose objects are
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  of length
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ←
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ←
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ←
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X = X_0 \leftarrow X_1 \to X_2 \leftarrow \cdots \to X_{n-1} \leftarrow X_n = Y
                %p
                  such that each morphism going to the left,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi k
                          %mo ←
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi k
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{2k}\leftarrow X_{2k +1}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  morphisms between such objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,X_i,Y) \to (X',X'_i,Y')
                  are collections of weak equivalences
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i \to X'_i)
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi i
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt i \lt n
                  such that all triangles and squares commute.
          #HammockLocalization.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi wMor
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(wMor_C^n(X,Y))
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of this category, a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hammock+localization"} hammock localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi L
                      %mi W
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W^H C
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
              with objects those of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over the length of these hammock hom-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo →
                          %mi n
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi wMor
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^H C(X,Y) := \lim_{\to_n} N(wMor_C^n(X,Y))
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
              of this simplicial set is the derived hom-space between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              of the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
          %h3#Framings For a model category
          %p
            The derived hom spaces of a model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            may always be computed in terms of simplicial resolutions with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
            %em framings
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hovey"}> Hovey
            ). These constructions are originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#DHK"}> Dwyer-Hirschhorn-Kan
            ).
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ×
                          %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mo •
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ev
                              %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi const
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (const \dashv ev_0 \dashv (-)^{\times^\bullet})
                    \:
                    C
                    \\stackrel{\overset{const}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{ev_0}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{(-)^{\times^\bullet}}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\,,
                    [\Delta^{op}, C]
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi const
                        %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const X : [n] \mapsto X
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ev
                          %mn 0
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_0 X_\bullet = X_0
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ×
                              %mo •
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↦
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\times^\bullet} : [n] \mapsto X^{\times^{n+1}}
                  \.
          #CoDiscreteIsReedyFibrant.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              fibrant,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ×
                          %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\times^\bullet}
              is fibrant in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The matching morphisms are in fact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a model category.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
                  any object, a
                  %em simplicial frame
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is a factorization of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi const
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ×
                              %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const X \to X^{\times^\bullet}
                  into a weak equivalence followed by a fibration in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi Reedy
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %em right framing
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is a functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo •
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_\bullet :  C \to [\Delta^{op}, C]
                  with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X)_0 \simeq X
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  is a simplicial frame on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Dually for
              = succeed "." do
                %em cosimplicial frames
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Hovey"}> Hovey, def. 5.2.7
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoDiscreteIsReedyFibrant"}
              a simplicial frame
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              in the above is in particular fibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
          #SimplicialFunctionComplexes.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              fibrant, there are weak equivalences in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi diag
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_C(X^\bullet, A)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    diag Hom_C(X^\bullet, A_\bullet)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}
                    Hom_C(X, A_\bullet)
                    \\,,
            %p
              (where in the middle we have the diagonal of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X^\bullet, A_\bullet)
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Hovey"}> Hovey, prop. 5.4.7
            ).
          %p
            Either of these simplicial sets is a model for the derived hom-space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Hom(X,A)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              By developing these constructions further, one obtains a canonical
              = succeed "-resolution" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "fibrant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
              = succeed "-hom" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#EnrichedHomsCofToFib"} below
            %p
              This is discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category#SimpEquivMods"} Simplicial Quillen equivalent models
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a model category, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{c}_\mathrm{w} C
              be the full subcategory of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta, C]
              spanned by the cosimplicial objects whose coface and codegeneracy operators are weak equivalences, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} s
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{s}_\mathrm{w} C
              be the full subcategory of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
              spanned by the simplicial objects whose face and degeneracy operators are weak equivalences.
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const : C \to \mathrm{c}_\mathrm{w} C
                is the right half of an adjoint homotopical equivalence of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} s
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const : C \to \mathrm{s}_\mathrm{w} C
                is the left half of an adjoint homotopical equivalence of homotopical categories.
              %li
                The functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} diag
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} c
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                      %mi C
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} s
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} w
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{diag} Hom_C : (\mathrm{c}_\mathrm{w} C)^{op} \times \mathrm{s}_\mathrm{w} C \to sSet
                admits a right
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              %li
                The induced functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ho
                      %mi C
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ho
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ho
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\operatorname{Ho} C)^{op} \times \operatorname{Ho} C \to \operatorname{Ho} sSet
                is the derived hom-space functor.
          %h3#EnrichedHomsCofToFib For a simplicial model category
          %p
            We describe here in more detail properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-functors"} derived hom-functors
            (see there for more) in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          %p
            The crucial axiom used for this is the axiom of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            which says that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensor operation
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ×
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\cdot : C \times SSet \to C
              %p
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
            %li
              %p
                or equivalently that for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
                a cofibration and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                a fibration the induced morphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C(Y, A) \to C(X,A) \times_{C(X,B)} C(Y,B)
              %p
                is a fibration, which is acyclic if either
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                is.
          %p
            First of all the first statement directly implies that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \in C
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
            any object, the simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\emptyset,A) = {*}
            is the terminal simplicial set (see also
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "powered+and+copowered+category#InTensoredCotensoredCategoryInitialObjectIsEnrichedInitial"} this Prop.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi SSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ∅
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ∅
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mi ∅
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ∅
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  SSet(S,C(\emptyset, A))
                  \&amp; =  Hom_C(\emptyset \cdot S, A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = Hom_C(colim_{\emptyset} \cdot S, A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = Hom_C(\emptyset, A)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;= {*}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where we use that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
            is required to respect
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
          %p
            Similarly one has for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,{*}) = {*}
          %p Using this, the second equivalent form of the enrichment axiom has as a special case the following statement.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              fibrant, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,A)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We apply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              axiom to the cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
              and the fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to {*}
              to obtain a fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ,
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(X,A) \to C(\emptyset, A) \times_{C(\emptyset,{*})} C(X,{*})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The right hand is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of the terminal simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} = \Delta^0
              to itself, hence is itself the point. So we have a fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,A) \to {*}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,A)
              is a fibrant object in the standard
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              a fibration, the morphism of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,f) : C(X,A) \to C(X,B)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              that is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is acyclic.
            %p
              Dually, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : X \to Y
              a cofibration and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              fibrant, the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(i,A) : C(X,A) \to C(Y,A)
              is a cofibration of simplicial sets.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p This is as before. Explicity, consider the first case, the second one is the formal dual of that:
            %p
              We enter the enrichment axiom with the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              and find for the required
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mo *
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\emptyset,A) \times_{C(\emptyset, B)} C(X,B)
                    \=
                    {*} \times_{*} C(X,B)
                    \=
                    C(X,B)
            %p
              and hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,A) \to C(X,B)
              is, indeed, a fibration, which is acyclic if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is.
          .num_proposition
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a cofibant object and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}  B
            %p
              a weak equivalence between fibrant objects, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(X,f) : C(X,A) \to C(X,B)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              of
              = succeed "es." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %p
              Similarly, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a fibrant object and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Y
              a weak equivalence between cofibrant objects, the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(j,A) : C(X,A) \to C(Y,A)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              of
              = succeed "es." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p The second case is formally dual to the first, so we restrict attention to the first one.
            %p
              By the above, the axioms of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              ensure that the above statement is true when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is in addition a fibration. So we reduce the situation to that case.
            %p
              This is possible because both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are assumed to be fibrant. This allows to apply the
              %em factorization lemma
              that is described in great detail at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              between fibrant objects there is a commutative diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi E
                              %mi f
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi fib
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi W
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi fib
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{E}_f B
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\in fib \cap W}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\in fib}}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is assumed a weak equivalence it follows by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_f B
              is also a weak equivalence.
            %p
              Therefore by the above properties of simpliciall enriched categories we obtain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              of acyclic fibrations of
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}
                    C(X, \mathbf{E}_f B)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    C(X,B)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
              every weak equivalence of Kan complexes is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} C(X,\mathbf{E}_f B) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} C(X,B)
            %p
              that is homotopic to our
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,f)
          %h3#comparison Comparison
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialFunctionComplexes"}
            are related to the simplicial localization from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZigZagCategories"}
            and def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HammockLocalization"}
          %p
            Suppose now that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q : C \to C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement+functor"} cofibrant replacement functor
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : C \to C
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement+functor"} fibrant replacement functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi cC
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^\bullet : C \to (cC)_c
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+resolution+functor"} cosimplicial resolution functor
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sC
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_\bullet : C \to (sC)_f
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+resolution+functor"} simplicial resolution functor
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          #DKTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Dwyer–Kan)
            %p
              There are natural weak equivalences between the following equivalent realizations of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Mor
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mo •
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
