                    \\,.
          %p
            The top row weak equivalences are those of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialFunctionComplexes"}
          %h3#InACategoryOfFibrantObjects In a category of fibrant objects
          %p
            There is also an explicit simplicial construction of the derived hom spaces for a homotopical category that is equipped with the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Cisinski10"} Cisinksi 10
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#NSS12"} Nikolaus-Schreiber-Stevenson 12, section 3.6.2
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#SpacesOfEquivalences Hom-spaces of equivalences
          #DKTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an object, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aut_W(X) \subset \mathbb{R}Hom(X,X)
            %p
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of the component on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C_W)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of weak equivalences:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi W
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B} Aut_W(X) \simeq N(C_W)_X
                    \\,.
            %p
              The equivalence is given by a finite sequence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zags"} zig-zags
              and is natural with respect to
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
              of simplicial model categories that preserve weak equivalences and send a fibrant cofibrant model for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              again to a fibrant cofibrant object.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DK84"} Dwyer-Kan 84, 2.3, 2.4
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a model category, the simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C_W)
              is a model for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              determined by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              That core, like every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              is equivalent to the disjoint union over its connected components of the deloopings of the automorphism
              = succeed "-groups" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
