          %h2#references References
          %p
            For some original references by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Kan"} Dan Kan
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
          %ul
            %li#DK84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Kan"} Dan Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em A classification theorem for diagrams of simplicial sets
          %p
            On the derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+complexes"} function complexes
            in a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} projective model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Function complexes for diagrams of simplicial sets
              %strong 86
              2 (1983) 139-147 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/1385-7258(83)90051-3"}> doi:10.1016/1385-7258(83)90051-3
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82652265.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , Section 1.2.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/titles/8957.html"} pup:8957
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Dugger"}> Dan Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Spivak"} David Spivak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mapping spaces in quasi-categories
                %strong 11
                (2011) 263–325 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.0469"}> arXiv:0911.0469
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/agt.2011.11.263"} doi:10.2140/agt.2011.11.263
          %p
            The theory of
            %em framings
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#DHK
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"} Philip Hirschhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Kan"} Dan Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model categories and general abstract homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mimuw.edu.pl/~jacho/literatura/ModelCategory/DHK_ModelCateogories1.pdf"} pdf
          %p and in parallel section 5 of
          %ul
            %li#Hovey
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              ,
              %em Model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~brunov/SecretPassage/Hovey-Model%20Categories.ps"}> ps
              )
          %p and in sections 16, 17 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"}> Philip Hirschhorn
              ,
              %em Model categories and their localization
              \.
          %p A useful quick review of the interrelation of the various constructions of derived hom spaces is page 14, 15 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              %em On (enriched) left Bousfield localization of model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2067"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            Discussion of derived hom spaces for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+fibrant+objects"} categories of fibrant objects
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Cisinski10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invariance de la K-théorie par equivalences dérivées
          %p and section 3.6.2 of
          %ul
            %li#NSS12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
